# Build outputs (regenerated by axon-peripheral-sdk build), one per profile:
#   <profile>-devkit/build/
build/

# Build-time generated SV (regenerated by `make` on every build)
**/src/git_hash.sv
**/src/version.sv

# Radiant implementation scratch, emitted next to the project sources
**/src/impl_1/
**/src/promote.xml
**/src/promote.pfl
radiantc.log.*
radiantc.tcl.*

# Per-peripheral stubs the SDK scaffolder re-creates inside each profile
# project. `generate` emits src/<name>_peripheral.sv, test/tb/<name>_tb.sv and
# test/tb/test_<name>.py at those fixed paths whenever they're absent
# (project_scaffold.scaffold_new_peripheral) — it looks only at the convention,
# never at fpga.sources. Our RTL and tests are shared by both profiles and live
# one level up, so those stubs are dead weight: the generated .rdf compiles
# ../../axon_test_source_peripheral.sv, not the stub. Ignored rather than
# committed because the stub declares the SAME module name as a bare loopback,
# and a second definition in the tree is a trap for linters, editor indexes,
# and anything that globs src/*.sv. Delete them freely.
*-devkit/src/*_peripheral.sv
*-devkit/test/

# Python
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.pyo

# Cocotb sim artifacts
sim_build_*/
**/results.xml
